{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1790415631728,"sessionID":"ses_f22eb6cd1ffeAw9sRfWIkAPu1R","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_84e88f5b05bd42f2a915fa7c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Explore project structure","prompt":"Explore the /workspace directory thoroughly. I need to understand:\n1. The full directory structure (all files and folders)\n2. The main scene file(s)\n3. Any existing minimap-related code\n4. Any player, mob, crate scripts\n5. The world/main scene structure\n\nReturn a comprehensive summary of all files found, their paths, and their contents (especially .gd, .tscn, and project.godot files). Be very thorough - read every relevant file.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_f22eb30bbffeq3lcMrU20utsNP\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\nHere is a comprehensive summary of everything in `/workspace`:\n\n---\n\n## 1. FULL DIRECTORY STRUCTURE\n\n```\n/workspace/\n├── .godot/\n│   ├── .gdignore\n│   ├── global_script_class_cache.cfg\n│   ├── scene_groups_cache.cfg\n│   ├── uid_cache.bin\n│   └── editor/\n│       ├── filesystem_cache10\n│       ├── project_metadata.cfg\n│       └── main.tscn-folding-3ad5c15c4f3250da0cc7c1af1770d85f.cfg\n├── assets/\n│   ├── minimapIcon_arrowA.png\n│   ├── minimapIcon_arrowA.png.import\n│   ├── minimapIcon_arrowA.res           (binary)\n│   ├── minimapIcon_exclamationYellow.png\n│   ├── minimapIcon_exclamationYellow.png.import\n│   ├── minimapIcon_exclamationYellow.res (binary)\n│   ├── minimapIcon_jewelRed.png\n│   ├── minimapIcon_jewelRed.png.import\n│   ├── minimapIcon_jewelRed.res          (binary)\n│   ├── panel_woodDetail_blank.png\n│   ├── panel_woodDetail_blank.png.import\n│   ├── panel_woodDetail_blank.res       (binary)\n│   ├── pattern_blueprintPaper.png\n│   ├── pattern_blueprintPaper.png.import\n│   └── pattern_blueprintPaper.res       (binary)\n├── scenes/\n│   ├── crate.tscn\n│   ├── main.tscn\n│   ├── minimap.tscn\n│   ├── mob.tscn\n│   └── player.tscn\n├── scripts/\n│   ├── crate.gd\n│   ├── crate.gd.uid\n│   ├── minimap.gd\n│   ├── minimap.gd.uid\n│   ├── mob.gd\n│   ├── mob.gd.uid\n│   ├── player.gd\n│   ├── player.gd.uid\n│   ├── world.gd\n│   └── world.gd.uid\n├── project.godot\n└── task_config.json\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. PROJECT CONFIGURATION -- `/workspace/project.godot`\n\n- **Engine**: Godot 4.4, using `gl_compatibility` renderer\n- **Project name**: \"Minimap marker logic and zoom control\"\n- **Main scene**: `res://scenes/main.tscn`\n- **Config version**: 5\n\n---\n\n## 3. TASK DESCRIPTION -- `/workspace/task_config.json`\n\nThe task instruction reads:\n\n> \"Implement the minimap logic: export a Player reference and a zoom property with a clamped setter, cache the grid and marker prototypes, center the player marker after the first frame, compute grid_scale from the grid size and viewport, duplicate and show markers for every node in the minimap_objects group using their minimap_icon keys, store them in a 'markers' dictionary, rotate (player rotation + PI/2) and position markers each frame relative to the player (scaling to 0.75 and clamping when off the grid), implement `_on_object_removed` which removes and erases markers when called, and implement `_on_gui_input` which handles mouse wheel gui_input to adjust zoom. Ensure the world scene connects minimap_objects \"removed\" signals to the minimap while mobs/crates have the \"removed\" signals, expose each one's \"minimap_icon\", and ensure mobs/crates belong to the minimap_objects group.\"\n\n---\n\n## 4. MAIN SCENE -- `/workspace/scenes/main.tscn`\n\n**Type**: `Node2D` with `world.gd` script attached.\n\n**Node tree**:\n```\nMain (Node2D) [script: world.gd]\n├── CanvasLayer\n│   └── Minimap (MarginContainer) [instance of minimap.tscn]\n├── Player (CharacterBody2D) [instance of player.tscn, position: (0,0)]\n├── Mobs (Node2D)\n│   └── Mob (CharacterBody2D) [instance of mob.tscn, position: (120,0)]\n└── Crates (Node2D)\n    └── Crate (Area2D) [instance of crate.tscn, position: (-160,0)]\n```\n\nKey observations:\n- The minimap lives inside a `CanvasLayer` (ensures it renders as overlay).\n- The Player, Mobs container, and Crates container are siblings under Main.\n- Exactly one Mob at `(120, 0)` and one Crate at `(-160, 0)` exist at scene load.\n\n---\n\n## 5. MINIMAP SCENE -- `/workspace/scenes/minimap.tscn`\n\n**Type**: `MarginContainer`  \n**Size**: 200x200 pixels  \n**Resources loaded**: 5 textures (panel wood, blueprint paper, arrow, jewel, exclamation)\n\n**Node tree**:\n```\nMinimap (MarginContainer) [200x200, 5px margins]\n├── Frame (NinePatchRect) [texture: panel_woodDetail_blank, 64px patch margins]\n├── Content (MarginContainer) [20px margins]\n    └── Grid (TextureRect) [texture: pattern_blueprintPaper, stretch_mode=Tile]\n        ├── PlayerMarker (Sprite2D) [texture: minimapIcon_arrowA, pos: (75,75), visible]\n        ├── MobMarker (Sprite2D) [texture: minimapIcon_jewelRed, pos: (24,24), HIDDEN]\n        └── AlertMarker (Sprite2D) [texture: minimapIcon_exclamationYellow, pos: (120,120), HIDDEN]\n```\n\nKey observations for minimap implementation:\n- The `Grid` has `stretch_mode = 1` (Tile), which matters for grid_scale computation.\n- `PlayerMarker` is visible (the arrow icon, meant to rotate with the player).\n- `MobMarker` and `AlertMarker` are hidden prototypes to be duplicated for each actual mob/crate.\n- Three distinct marker icons exist:\n  - `minimapIcon_arrowA` -- for the player (green arrow)\n  - `minimapIcon_jewelRed` -- for mobs (red jewel/diamond)\n  - `minimapIcon_exclamationYellow` -- for crates/alerts (yellow exclamation)\n\n---\n\n## 6. PLAYER -- `/workspace/scenes/player.tscn` + `/workspace/scripts/player.gd`\n\n**Scene**: A `CharacterBody2D` with `player.gd` attached.\n\n**Script** (`/workspace/scripts/player.gd`):\n```gdscript\nextends CharacterBody2D\nclass_name Player\n\nvar speed := 120.0\nvar rotation_speed := 2.0\n\nfunc _physics_process(delta):\n    velocity = transform.x * speed * delta\n    move_and_slide()\n```\n- The player moves forward along its `transform.x` axis (rightward in local space).\n- Has `speed` (120.0) and `rotation_speed` (2.0) but no rotation input logic yet.\n- Class is registered globally as `Player` (extends `CharacterBody2D`).\n- **Missing**: No `minimap_icon` property and no `removed` signal.\n\n---\n\n## 7. MOB -- `/workspace/scenes/mob.tscn` + `/workspace/scripts/mob.gd`\n\n**Scene**: A `CharacterBody2D` with `mob.gd` attached.\n\n**Script** (`/workspace/scripts/mob.gd`):\n```gdscript\nextends CharacterBody2D\nclass_name Mob\n\n# TODO: add minimap_icon + removed signal and movement logic\n```\n- Class is registered globally as `Mob`.\n- **Missing**: `minimap_icon` variable, `removed` signal, movement logic, and `minimap_objects` group membership.\n\n---\n\n## 8. CRATE -- `/workspace/scenes/crate.tscn` + `/workspace/scripts/crate.gd`\n\n**Scene**: An `Area2D` with `crate.gd` attached.\n\n**Script** (`/workspace/scripts/crate.gd`):\n```gdscript\nextends Area2D\nclass_name Crate\n\n# TODO: emit a removed signal and expose minimap_icon once hooked up to minimap\n```\n- Class is registered globally as `Crate` (extends `Area2D`).\n- Unlike Mob/Player, Crate is not a physics body -- it is a detection area.\n- **Missing**: `minimap_icon` variable, `removed` signal, and `minimap_objects` group membership.\n\n---\n\n## 9. WORLD SCRIPT -- `/workspace/scripts/world.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nextends Node2D\n\nfunc _ready():\n    pass # TODO: wire removed signals and minimap player reference\n```\n- Attached to the `Main` node in `main.tscn`.\n- **Missing**: Getting the Minimap node, wiring signals from mobs/crates to the minimap, setting the minimap's player reference.\n\n---\n\n## 10. MINIMAP SCRIPT -- `/workspace/scripts/minimap.gd`\n\n```gdscript\nextends MarginContainer\n\n# TODO: implement minimap marker logic, zoom control, and removal handling\n```\n- Attached to the `Minimap` node in `minimap.tscn`.\n- **Missing**: Everything -- `@export var player`, `@export var zoom`, grid/marker caching in `_ready()`, marker duplication/creation from `minimap_objects` group, per-frame marker positioning/rotation/scaling/clamping in `_process()`, `_on_object_removed()`, and `_on_gui_input()`.\n\n---\n\n## 11. ASSET FILES\n\n| File | Purpose |\n|---|---|\n| `assets/minimapIcon_arrowA.png` | Player marker (green arrow) |\n| `assets/minimapIcon_jewelRed.png` | Mob marker (red jewel/diamond) |\n| `assets/minimapIcon_exclamationYellow.png` | Crate/alert marker (yellow exclamation) |\n| `assets/panel_woodDetail_blank.png` | Frame border texture (NinePatchRect) |\n| `assets/pattern_blueprintPaper.png` | Grid background texture (blueprint paper) |\n\nEach `.png.import` file configures the texture with no mipmaps, default lossless compression, and alpha border fixing. Each `.res` file is a Godot binary resource (the imported `CompressedTexture2D`).\n\n---\n\n## 12. GODOT CACHE FILES\n\n- `/workspace/.godot/global_script_class_cache.cfg`: Registers three global script classes -- `Crate` (extends `Area2D`), `Mob` (extends `CharacterBody2D`), `Player` (extends `CharacterBody2D`). No world or minimap class is registered.\n- `/workspace/.godot/scene_groups_cache.cfg`: Empty -- no groups registered yet (e.g., `minimap_objects` group does not yet exist).\n- `/workspace/.godot/editor/project_metadata.cfg`: Shows Godot executable path and recent files (`main.tscn`).\n\n---\n\n## 13. SUMMARY OF WHAT NEEDS IMPLEMENTATION\n\nBased on the task_config instruction, the codebase is a skeleton where nearly all logic is stubbed out with TODO comments. The implementation plan is:\n\n1. **`scripts/player.gd`**: Unchanged (no minimap-specific work needed here).\n2. **`scripts/mob.gd`**: Add `signal removed`, `var minimap_icon`, movement logic.\n3. **`scripts/crate.gd`**: Add `signal removed`, `var minimap_icon`.\n4. **`scripts/world.gd`** (`_ready`): Get the Minimap node, set its `player` ref, connect each mob/crate's `removed` signal to `_on_object_removed`.\n5. **`scripts/minimap.gd`**: The main file -- export `player` (Player type) and `zoom`, cache `$Content/Grid` and marker prototypes in `_ready()`, duplicate markers for `minimap_objects` group members in the first frame via `await get_tree().process_frame`, compute `grid_scale`, position/rotate/scale markers each `_process`, clamp off-grid markers, handle `_on_object_removed()`, and handle `_on_gui_input()` for mouse wheel zoom.\n6. **`scenes/mob.tscn` and `scenes/crate.tscn`**: Add `minimap_objects` group membership (in Godot editor or via tscn editing).\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_f22eb6cd1ffeAw9sRfWIkAPu1R","sessionId":"ses_f22eb30bbffeq3lcMrU20utsNP","model":{"modelID":"deepseek-v4-pro","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Explore project structure","time":{"start":1790415523657,"end":1790415631718}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_6561ebf8-a114-466c-9db1-98e19d4c132b"}},"id":"prt_0dd14cf39001TJkxGNjCqSixca","sessionID":"ses_f22eb6cd1ffeAw9sRfWIkAPu1R","messageID":"msg_0dd1495700018vu7ge6Eukh90s"}}
